{
  "slug": "ix-memory",
  "name": "Ix Memory",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Ix Memory connects Claude Code to Ix, a structured, persistent memory backend for codebases. Instead of reading raw source files to answer questions about your code, Claude queries a live knowledge graph — dramatically reducing token usage, improving accuracy, and enabling reasoning that scales to large, complex projects.\nAll analysis runs locally on your machine. No source code is ever transmitted to external servers.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**, **5 agents** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `ix-architecture` (Analyze system design — structure, coupling, code smells, and high-risk hotspots), `ix-debug` (Root cause analysis — trace execution path to a failure, narrow candidates, read minimal source only at suspected…), `ix-docs` (Generate narrative-first, importance-weighted documentation for a repo, system, or subsystem with a selective reference layer), `ix-impact` (Change risk analysis — blast radius, affected systems, and what to test), `ix-investigate` (Deep dive into a symbol, feature, or bug), `ix-plan` (Generate a risk-ordered implementation plan for a set of targets), `ix-understand` (Build a detailed architectural mental model of a system, subsystem, or the whole repo)\n- **Agents** (5): `ix-architecture-auditor` (Analyzes system design quality — coupling, cohesion, smells, hotspots), `ix-bug-investigator` (Root cause analysis agent), `ix-explorer` (General-purpose codebase exploration agent), `ix-safe-refactor-planner` (Generates a risk-ordered refactor plan with safe edit boundaries), `ix-system-explorer` (Builds a complete architectural mental model of a codebase or subsystem)\n- **Hooks** (4): `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ix-memory@claude-community` from `ix-infrastructure/ix-claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 7,
    "agent": 5,
    "hook": 4
  },
